{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART sent 0xa5 but recv_buf_data latched 0xd2, causing TRAP uart data mismatch and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause is duplicate case label 0 in recv_state case: the half-bit start-center wait (2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) is labeled 0 instead of 1 so state 1 is dead and falls to default full-bit wait. This half-bit sampling offset corrupts received bits.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -78,10 +78,10 @@
 			0: begin
 				if (!ser_rx)
 					recv_state <= 1;
 				recv_divcnt <= 0;
 			end
-			0: begin
+			1: begin
 				if (2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 					recv_state <= 2;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
 			end
", "expected": "tohost: PASS, uart loopback 0xa5 matches, no TRAP uart data mismatch"}

